:So, when you are confused, KNOW WHAT YOU ARE DOING when you read a
:scroll. Unidentified scrolls are always dangerous, and anything you have never 
:read-while-confused before might generate unpredictable results.
     Actually, I posted the effects of all the scrolls while one is confused
a while ago.  Genocide scrolls are vcery dangerous, but apart from those
and teleport scrolls, you're quite safe reading a scroll while confused
(as long as you can handle 10 grid bugs at a time; being confused while
reading a scroll of create monster *will* create ten monsters, prompting
you for a monster name each time.  If it's cursed, you might be in trouble,
however.  Kind of a small risk.)  So if you've already found a genocide
and teleport scroll, it can actually be a pretty good means of figuring
things out.  You lose the effect of an identify scroll (but identify it as
one), and a confuse monster scroll (big deal).  Destroy armor scrolls have
no effect whatsoever-- a pretty big plus, actually ("Your armor grows
purple.  Call a scroll labelled DUAM XNAH:").  Enchant scrolls rustproof
(if you've used your genocide scroll to get rid of rust monsters, this
might not be as good as the vanilla enchant scroll, but it protects, I
believe, against cursed scrolls, and if it's an enchant weapon scroll, you
still have some big plusses as far as being able to attack things.)

     By the way, has anyone ever been killed by a gelatinous cube?  I've
found that you don't get paralyzed as long as you don't attack them, so if
it's doubling up on you with something else, you can kill the something else
and then turn your attentions towards the cube, unless you're low on hp.

